[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Indian Defence"]
[Variation "Samisch Variation"]
[ECO "E81"]
[Character "sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "e5-break,queenside-attack"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. f3 { A solid pawn chain, supporting e4 and preparing Be3 and long castling. } 5... O-O
6. Be3 e5 { Hits d4 straight away. Black fights for the centre before White's pieces are all out. }
7. Nge2 ( 7. d5 Nh5 { Heads for f4 and prepares ...f5. } 8. Qd2 f5 9. O-O-O Na6 )
( 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Nd5 Nxd5 10. cxd5 c6 { Attacks the d5 pawn and opens the position for the bishop pair. } )
7... c6 { Keeps knights out of d5 and prepares ...a6 and ...b5. } 8. Qd2 Nbd7 { Develops and defends e5. }
9. O-O-O a6 { Prepares ...b5. White's king is on the queenside, so a pawn storm there is a real threat. }
10. Kb1 b5 { The pawn storm starts. The pawn threatens to hit c4 and open lines against the king. } *
